  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Among <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>Ti</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> ions, one if used as a reagent cannot liberate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> from dilute mineral acid solution, its spin-only magnetic moment in gaseous state is _____&nbsp; B.M. (Nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Among the given species&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;cannot undergo oxidation, hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> can&#39;t liberate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>It has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;configuration,</p><p>Number of unpaired electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>92</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.&#160;</mo></math></p></blockquote>",
